@rekram1-node I used the term "lobotomizing" because that has been my experience with OpenCode recently: this has led to a substantial degradation in performance for anything that runs past compaction. If an agent has 10 things to do and gets stuck debugging item 5, then hits compaction, then continues, it's a coin toss whether it magically remembers the other 5 items or just spits out the celebratory self-congratulations on solving half the task because it can't remember the other half. When it had the todoread tool, it regularly used it to pick up the remaining items. Hence, this change has lobotomized OpenCode.

Edit: I don't know what "further improvements" you had in mind, but it doesn't seem like any of them exist in OpenCode yet, so removing the one thing that helped with long running tasks before making the other improvements is at the very least an exercise in poor judgment and project management.

Edit 2: Just because all the other lemmings are jumping off a cliff doesn't mean you should follow suit.
